---
import Frame from '../components/PageFrame.astro';

const items = [
  {
    title: 'A practical SME operations guide',
    body: 'Map one recurring request with a trigger, owner and condition for every hand-off.',
  },
  {
    title: 'The value of a usable website',
    body: 'Evaluate the experience against what customers need to understand and do.',
  },
  {
    title: 'What to measure, and why',
    body: 'Choose clearly defined indicators that help a person make a decision.',
  },
];
---

<Frame label="Journal" items={items}>
  <section class="container section" id="editorial-context">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">ORIGINAL FIELD NOTES</p>
      <h2>Useful ideas. Clear examples.</h2>
      <p>
        Three practical guides on everyday operations and website experience.
        Read the explanation, try the related local demo and adapt the checklist
        to your own context. No customer outcomes or search-volume claims.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container section split-section">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">READ WITH CONTEXT</p>
      <h2>Good questions travel further than dashboards.</h2>
      <p>
        A process map can start on paper. A useful metric starts with a
        decision. A redesign starts with the visitor’s needs. The guides aim to
        help before they invite you anywhere else.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="reading">
      <h3>Operations and website experience</h3>
      <p>
        Operations notes explain ownership, approval and reporting using
        fictional examples. Website notes connect those interface lessons to a
        real business website: readable content, mobile usability, accessible
        controls and truthful measurement.
      </p>
      <h3>Sources and editorial care</h3>
      <p>
        Technical guidance links to primary sources where appropriate. The
        byline identifies ISMAIL as the project’s creator; the articles do not
        claim first-hand client studies or measured commercial results.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/technology/">
        Understand the implementation behind the examples →
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Frame>
